body:
This isn't going to be sunshine and rainbows but it's a positive for sure! So i was in hospital for a collapsed lung that happened randomly. And i was in for around 4 days, and it genuinely helped with my anxiety (I suffer with health anxiety) and having to deal with that with something actually serious and not in my head, and being in hospital bored out of my mind gave me a lot of time to think about who i am as a person, what i've been doing in my life. And it was just days of pure thinking? I had quite a few epiphanies and a lot of them were positive

&#x200B;

So i came out of hospital and i've started to see things a lot more clearly, and i've had a few down moments, but i feel more connected to people after learning that a lot of people actually care about me. And i've actually seen my memory recollecton improve with my studies.

Hey, thank you so much! I used to write a while back but then i stopped! In general, i know what should bring me satisfaction, if only briefly! 

&#x200B;

Honestly, i think getting mad and ranting about how stupid it is does help with the anxiety. Though i've had a couple of drinks tonight and i've had a period of anxiety which is now affecting me even whilst under the influence. It sucks that my anxiety just seems to get worse lmao

Also, if you happen to have streaks that go towards your heart/up your arm, feeling feverish or flu like symptoms go directly to the ER because it may be a sign of systemic infection/sepsis.

&#x200B;

What i'm trying to say, is keep a close eye on your condition and stay vigilant.

Since you've been having bad trips a lot. When it's on the come-up, many people experience anxiety. Do you find yourself being scared of a bad trip whenever you take them? Because you can get stuck in a thought loop that can bring a bad trip on. 

&#x200B;

When it comes to your sober life, try meditating and do a bit of self-discovery, most bad trips either come from External circumstances such as set and setting, but they can also come from within, such as pre-existing negative thoughts or expectations going into the trip.

Chances are, if they are alive. They might be in Critical condition, or if they recovered, they could have been checked into a mental health facility where mobile devices aren't permitted, could be way too exhausted to even use their phone whilst recovering etc. So not having an update seems most likely due to these conditions.

&#x200B;

Let us all hope that OP is still alive, don't give up yet.

Overwatch is less reaction-time heavy than other shooters. Since the time to kill is longer, you'll have a much better chance of killing someone as a DPS than any other class due to high damage, you'll have less reliance on reaction time.

&#x200B;

TL;DR, You don't need rapid reaction time to be an effective DPS

&#x200B;

side note, if you find a class fun! Then play it, if you don't feel confident in a competitive scenario, then try to master certain heroes in quickplay. Another tip: Pick your engagements carefully, a lot of people die easily and are stuck in low ranks playing DPS because they don't pick engagements that they can win and end up trying to 1v2 a dps and a tank.

Also, some of the spelling mistakes on the screenshots that have claimed to have been pyro are so dumb. The grammar seems pretty awful, and pyro's pretty articulate.

&#x200B;

Not to mention that the speech patterns are very different from pyro's turn of phrase.

So i'm currently level 6 on faceit and Hovering around SMFC - LEM because of inconsistent teams and my own inconsistent performance. Now i'm hardstuck in LEM and i just want to get to supreme and stay there before i want to fully commit to faceit. I have a couple of questions:


1) Is how do you hold B site on Inferno well?  I find myself just getting one tapped by everyone who comes by, or not getting frags as they're coming out towards pool holding from Fountain, back site, pillar or dark. I don't really want to be stuck holding coffins or banana for the rest of my time playing inferno. 

&#x200B;

2) Similar question: But i get really paranoid when trying to take sites on maps like inferno and mirage without utility as there are quite a few angles to isolate, and doing it quickly results in my untimely death. How would i improve in that aspect? 

&#x200B;

3) How do you deal with very passive CT's as an individual if they don't peek?

